# The pre-auth walled garden: the ONLY hosts an unregistered device may reach.
#
# Deliberately not in allow.d/ -- these must resolve for everyone but be
# reachable only by devices that have not registered yet. A registered student
# is blocked from them, which is the point: www.google.com is Google search.
#
# Google's device flow is what makes this list necessary. It needs no redirect
# URI, which matters because Google refuses private-IP redirect targets, so a
# portal at 192.168.63.1 could never be one. The cost is that the code is
# entered at www.google.com/device.
accounts.google.com
www.google.com

# NOT the google.com apex. It was tried, and the query log showed exactly what
# suffix matching admits to a not-yet-registered device: mail.google.com,
# chat.google.com and play.google.com all resolved. Google Chat is a chat
# client, which integrity-policy.md bans during a session, so the apex costs
# more than the dead end it fixes.
#
# The portal therefore names the host explicitly -- https://www.google.com/device
# -- and a student can always approve the code from a phone instead, which is
# the reliable path when a laptop browser misbehaves.
www.gstatic.com
ssl.gstatic.com

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# YOUR INSTITUTION'S SINGLE SIGN-ON. Edit this part.
#
# A university Google account is usually federated: picking it at Google
# redirects to your own identity provider, and if that host is not reachable
# the student lands on "Safari can't find the server" holding a URL a mile
# long. Google's own hosts are not enough.
#
# Find yours by signing in once and watching the address bar, or run
# `classnet debug on`, attempt a sign-in, then `classnet log` -- it names every
# host that was refused.
#
# The whole institution domain, not one host, because the chain hops: Google
# sends you to idp.usfca.edu (Shibboleth), which hands off to usfcas.usfca.edu
# (CAS), which may hand off again. Chasing each hop means a student stranded on
# "Safari can't find the server" every time one changes.
#
# The cost: a not-yet-registered device can reach the university's own web
# pages. Registered devices cannot -- the garden is pre-auth only.
usfca.edu

# Multi-factor. Duo is the common pairing with a Shibboleth IdP; the per-tenant
# API host is a subdomain, which this covers.
duosecurity.com
